WEBVTT

00:21:58.208 --> 00:22:00.376
instead of saying, "That's not my job,"

00:22:00.400 --> 00:22:02.506
they're more likely to expand their roles

00:22:02.530 --> 00:22:06.266
to take the initiative
to develop and implement new ideas.

00:22:06.290 --> 00:22:07.644
With his manager's approval,

00:22:07.668 --> 00:22:09.982
Nico spent two months
building a computer program

00:22:10.006 --> 00:22:13.036
that would automate
how SAP processed invoice payments.

00:22:13.060 --> 00:22:15.386
When he was finished,
he ran some tests at work.

00:22:15.410 --> 00:22:17.447
The efficiency gains were huge.

00:22:17.471 --> 00:22:19.270
NN: It was really successful.

00:22:19.294 --> 00:22:21.113
We had three full days,

00:22:21.137 --> 00:22:24.496
and we reduced the time of processing
to just a couple of minutes.

00:22:24.520 --> 00:22:27.716
AG: Accounts payable started using
Nico's program regularly.

00:22:27.740 --> 00:22:29.147
Then a coworker nominated him

00:22:29.171 --> 00:22:31.386
for the Hasso Plattner Founders' Award,